    "question": "New York is two-thirds as populated as all of New England. If New England has 2100000 people, calculate the combined population of both states.",
    "gold": "3500000",
    "answer": "New York is two-thirds as populated as all of New England, meaning there are 2/3*2100000 = <<2/3*2100000=1400000>>1400000 people living in New York.\nThe combined population of both states is 1400000+2100000 = <<1400000+2100000=3500000>>3500000\n#### 3500000"
