  "generation": {
    "text": "To find the combined population of New York and New England, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Determine the population of New York.\n2. Add the population of New York to the population of New England.\n\nFirst, we know that New York is two-thirds as populated as all of New England. New England has a population of 2100000 people. Therefore, the population of New York is:\n\\[\n\\text{Population of New York} = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 2100000\n\\]\nTo calculate this, we perform the multiplication:\n\\[\n\\text{Population of New York} = \\frac{2 \\times 2100000}{3} = \\frac{4200000}{3} = 1400000\n\\]\nSo, the population of New York is 1400000 people.\n\nNext, we add the population of New York to the population of New England to find the combined population:\n\\[\n\\text{Combined population} = \\text{Population of New York} + \\text{Population of New England} = 1400000 + 2100000 = 3500000\n\\]\nTherefore, the combined population of New York and New England is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{3500000}\n\\]",
